<div class="grid three"><article class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Protein</div><h2>Food first. Powder if useful.</h2><p>Protein supports muscle repair and adaptation. Foods such as yogurt, beans, tofu, fish, and poultry can contribute throughout the day.</p><p class="quiet">A supplement can be convenient, but it is not necessary when food already meets your needs. Check ingredients and allergens.</p></article>
<article class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">02 / Creatine</div><h2>Useful for some training.</h2><p>Creatine can help repeated bursts of intense activity, such as lifting. Its benefits are less clear for endurance performance.</p><p class="quiet">Weight gain from water retention can occur. This preview offers no personal dosing plan; discuss suitability with a qualified professional.</p></article>
<article class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">03 / Caffeine</div><h2>Energy has a trade-off.</h2><p>Caffeine may improve some exercise performance, but responses vary. It can disrupt sleep and cause anxiety or a rapid heartbeat.</p><p class="quiet">More is not always better. Count all sources, including pre-workouts, coffee, and energy drinks.</p></article></div>
